@title Welcome to Customer Success
@subtitle A letter for the November 2026 cohort at Larkspur Software
@author Nadia Farouk, VP of Customer Success

Hello, and welcome!

We are so glad you are here. You are joining a team of 42 people spread across Denver, Dublin and Singapore, which means someone is almost always awake to help a customer, and to help you. We care a lot about our customers and about each other, and we like to keep things practical. This letter covers what to expect in your first days and months.

# Your first week

- **Monday**: laptop pickup at 09:00, followed by a welcome breakfast.
- **Tuesday**: a product deep dive with the Solutions team.
- **Wednesday**: shadow two customer calls.
- **Thursday**: support tooling training.
- **Friday**: lunch with your onboarding buddy.

# Your first 90 days

**By day 30**, your focus is learning the product. Ask questions, click through everything, and sit in on as many customer conversations as you can. Nobody expects you to know it all yet.

**By day 60**, you will own five accounts alongside your buddy. You will lead the conversations, and your buddy will be there to back you up and talk things through afterward.

**By day 90**, you will run quarterly business reviews on your own. By then you will know your accounts well, and you will have seen enough reviews to make them yours.

# People to know

- **Nadia Farouk**, VP of Customer Success
- **Owen Achterberg**, Head of Support
- **Priyanka Rao**, Enablement lead

! Tip: the `#cs-newbies` channel is the best place to ask anything. No question is too small.

We are glad you chose to spend this part of your career with us. Take your time, be curious, and say hello often.

See you on Monday,

Nadia Farouk
VP of Customer Success
